# ---- GOLDEN FIXTURE (bridge tile) ----
# resetMode=loadvm -> restore the INTERNAL 'golden' snapshot: X (-nocursor) +
# MAME 0.289 `zx81` at the machine's own untouched power-on screen. There was
# never a curated alternative to weigh up here: a ZX81 prints NO banner, no
# memory count and no copyright line, so its empty white field with one inverse
# `K` is the only screen that is unambiguously the machine's own rather than
# something a previous visitor left behind.
SH_RESET_MODE=loadvm
SH_GOLDEN_SNAPSHOT=golden
SH_FIXTURE_DESC=Sinclair ZX81 (1981) at its own untouched power-on screen: a white field with a single inverse-video K in the bottom-left corner and nothing else — no banner, no memory count, no copyright line. K is the machine telling you it is in keyword mode, where one keypress enters a whole BASIC word (P gives PRINT). MAME 0.289 zx81 with -bios 2nd and -ramsize 1K, drawn fullscreen with aspect correction on the bridge kiosk's 1024x768 X root, which is exactly the 4:3 of the television the machine was sold to be plugged into. Keyboard-only exhibit; no pointer device; the ZX81 has no sound hardware, so the AC97 stream is silent by design.

# ---- KEYBOARD PACING (the exhibit's only input surface) ----
# 100/100, and the derivation was WRONG here — only the measurement holds.
#
# The playbook's rule is "two emulated frames": this driver runs at 50.655 Hz,
# so the frame is 19.74 ms and the floor would be 40/40. Measured on a clone of
# this tile (2026-08-09), typing a fixed 20-key line and counting the character
# cells the ZX81 actually painted, 20 keys per run:
#
#     hold=gap    keys landed (runs)
#      40 ms       1        (3 runs, identical)
#      60 ms       4-9      (5 runs)
#      80 ms      19-20     (5 runs, one imperfect)
#     100 ms      20/20     (13 runs, zero losses, 260 keys)
#     120 ms       8-18     (5 runs)
#     160 ms      13       (3 runs)
#     250 ms       8-14     (3 runs)
#
# That is a WINDOW, not a floor: this machine loses keys held too LONG as well
# as too briefly, which no other tile in the collection does and which the
# playbook's model does not predict. The mechanism was not identified (the
# ZX81 ROM's own keyboard debounce/repeat logic is the obvious suspect) — what
# is recorded here is the measurement, not a theory. 100/100 is the measured
# optimum and is what ships; do not "tidy" it towards the 40/40 derivation.
SH_KEY_MIN_HOLD_MS=100
SH_KEY_MIN_GAP_MS=100
# No SH_KEY_MAP. MAME's emulated-keyboard mode already maps host keys onto the
# ZX81's 40-key matrix, and the mapping a visitor most needs to understand is
# not a translation problem at all: at the `K` cursor the ZX81 is in KEYWORD
# mode, so pressing P does not type a letter, it enters the whole word PRINT.
# That is the machine, not a defect, and the SPA's zx81 keyboard profile shows
# the keyword legends the way the real key caps did.
